From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:49:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] kk: keep KK_WORKAROUND_11 on macOS 27, name compiling
 threads after their compile

STEAMAC-31/39. KosmicKrisp turned KK_WORKAROUND_11 (one MTL4Compiler per
MTLDevice, shared by every Vulkan device) off from macOS 27.0.0, as
FB22683138 (concurrent compiles on several MTL4Compilers corrupt the heap)
was fixed in macOS 27 beta 5. Betas 1-4 report 27.0.0 as well, and on them
virglrenderer, which creates an instance and a device per Venus context,
crashed in libmalloc's heap corruption trap: 4 crashes on beta 1 (26A5353q,
M4 Pro) and beta 4 (26A5388g, M3 Max), all within a second of a guest
session (re)starting, when gamescope, Xwayland and Steam create their devices
at once. In three of them two ring threads were in
newComputePipelineStateWithDescriptor: of kk_device_init_lib, each on its own
device's compiler, and both were freeing memory when the trap fired (inside
AGXMetalG16X, or in the autorelease pool popped after the call); a render
pipeline of the same user crashed with a protection fault inside AGX's
compiler in the same kind of burst. The workaround stays on: one shared
compiler compiles concurrently as fast as one per device (16 threads
compiling on an M1 Max, macOS 27.0.1: the same time either way).

Every Metal compile (library, compute or render pipeline) now names its
thread for as long as it runs: "kk <kind> <MSL hashes> compiler <n>: <k> in
flight on <m>" (MSL hashes as in MESA_KK_DEBUG=cbs, n the serial number of
the MTL4Compiler), so a crash report's thread list shows every compile in
flight, its compiler and how many ran at once. MESA_KK_DEBUG=compiles logs
each MTL4Compiler created and each compile with its thread, compiler,
duration and the most compiles and distinct compilers that overlapped it.

host/moltenvk/repro compilers.c: 8 threads create an instance and a device
each at the same moment and compile 16 compute pipelines each at the same
time; 0001-0046 on macOS 27: 8 MTL4Compilers, compiles on up to 8 at once;
now one, compiles still overlapping on it.
